[{:db/id "q-19981/selection/5262673284b7c302d3585c9002abfa6f78bc596dd7bbd88c14bc9a6c887b0e13" :answer/id #uuid "bb630e3b-7242-52f2-8105-dc8766c3ee8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19981/selection/d18a8dda3b8d65edd15eaec58978ca4092dbb278a54eb8bcb12a2dd65a77d732" :answer/id #uuid "67440ee5-3048-5442-9a5d-928011596213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19981/selection/e9fe03eb46cc37573ec616cc04dc0d03303ea19a17951a98b1d4a181cc97ecac" :answer/id #uuid "3d8acb3b-3c51-56d3-b4d3-ddd7eb354d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19981/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "11563b2f-3015-587d-a935-ff00f1aa98a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19981/selection/b070b6cf7e99a753b20eadee8f7b8de8260e882065588c6332866a0bf5de5668" :answer/id #uuid "02c30bad-b80f-5df4-8f05-e78884d0d444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19981/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0488a22f-bd62-5283-97d3-2169ba39a84d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19981/selection/d18a8dda3b8d65edd15eaec58978ca4092dbb278a54eb8bcb12a2dd65a77d732" :answer-field/choices ["q-19981/selection/5262673284b7c302d3585c9002abfa6f78bc596dd7bbd88c14bc9a6c887b0e13" "q-19981/selection/d18a8dda3b8d65edd15eaec58978ca4092dbb278a54eb8bcb12a2dd65a77d732" "q-19981/selection/e9fe03eb46cc37573ec616cc04dc0d03303ea19a17951a98b1d4a181cc97ecac" "q-19981/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" "q-19981/selection/b070b6cf7e99a753b20eadee8f7b8de8260e882065588c6332866a0bf5de5668"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19981" :question/id #uuid "348a27ba-92d1-50d2-bd80-7e9efcd9f74a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19981" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $u=⟨2,1,-1⟩$ and $v=⟨1,2,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-1))i-(2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,u\\times v\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-19981/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316350/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "dd674f8e-776e-5ee6-b3ed-a15767c27807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316350/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "090da758-6e1e-5777-ba60-de01ba856d66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316350/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae846422-472d-5a3b-8f96-4058155744b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316350/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-316350/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-316350/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316350" :question/id #uuid "59244d70-fcd7-573d-9e1f-295f7c2e83b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-316350" :question/problem "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨1,0,0⟩$ and $b=⟨0,3,4⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3)i-(1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =0i-4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316350/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580/selection/faad0727b2c62b6cced88abf9b210ea8763c2fd1c03c01c27346d66484992037" :answer/id #uuid "e02faf37-41e9-5afe-abb7-92aaf1831daf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "006222a6-687a-507d-96e2-1136e546b4f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580/selection/2e322c183dbc7d1ea89480e5179cfacfe0785b47fba2faa443ef41c049164964" :answer/id #uuid "c5f49e20-d837-5bb8-943a-55944a57aee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "d708ec19-b070-521e-9424-41650cc87725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "b7ea5528-010c-574a-84b3-f4e81b752bcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "73bd0eda-b458-56cc-8386-d9e0a1757bb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18580/selection/2e322c183dbc7d1ea89480e5179cfacfe0785b47fba2faa443ef41c049164964" :answer-field/choices ["q-18580/selection/faad0727b2c62b6cced88abf9b210ea8763c2fd1c03c01c27346d66484992037" "q-18580/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-18580/selection/2e322c183dbc7d1ea89480e5179cfacfe0785b47fba2faa443ef41c049164964" "q-18580/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" "q-18580/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18580" :question/id #uuid "608bfb63-b780-5090-a261-e63da05767db" :question/math-academy-id "q-18580" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $r=⟨1,-2,3⟩$ and $t=⟨0,1,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\times t & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,r\\times t\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18580/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18580"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275222/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer/id #uuid "d49f2234-eba2-5bff-8ba5-0680aa90047a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275222/field-1/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "c8cf0efc-1467-5a16-b24d-91d601bc9869" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275222/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd50816-269c-5e0b-8c44-0efba5dc358a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275222/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer-field/choices ["q-275222/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" "q-275222/field-1/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275222" :question/id #uuid "aed283df-d6ee-5f7a-b892-5e5d8815f8df" :question/math-academy-id "q-275222" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨-2,-1,0⟩$ and $b=⟨-4,2,-2⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0)i-((-2)\\cdot (-2)-(-4)\\cdot 0)j+((-2)\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =2i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275222/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275220/field-1/210215610152bc22dbe0958b830998dd4e50f2b6c40baf314cb7ba76c4d375cb" :answer/id #uuid "afbbd3c9-8108-58f6-9c5a-a485e3a3441f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275220/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5aed4cfb-e9ad-51e1-b67c-f4c2f55e42cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275220/field-1/210215610152bc22dbe0958b830998dd4e50f2b6c40baf314cb7ba76c4d375cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-275220/field-1/210215610152bc22dbe0958b830998dd4e50f2b6c40baf314cb7ba76c4d375cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275220" :question/id #uuid "c26b0a46-a1bf-5693-b2ed-f38811437f05" :question/math-academy-id "q-275220" :question/problem "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨-4,-2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,-2,-1⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-((-4)\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)j+((-4)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =4i-4j+8k \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275220/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866/selection/eda157d924643265f1a75a141081379a28abc5464ff0d5b66fe5078e6a946d39" :answer/id #uuid "56620c1c-6328-51a8-86fd-15180501d1cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{62}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866/selection/0a91f8a657eeb741a874acf8efeeecdbb5296f53af78027bc777d36c253a0f7f" :answer/id #uuid "d54af84f-cbbc-5372-ba07-e261c20bd3c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866/selection/385c7015fb21b22ceeda96a5b8f2b18de42db67284bafba3fabd3361d6d5baf4" :answer/id #uuid "8873aec4-e1a0-5c4f-97c2-ae8dd35eec80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866/selection/f0b130aae11871f8f940254091c645824b094093f8af351a9790e3a04cfe79fa" :answer/id #uuid "bdb6d05f-4105-5261-999b-ba078ba6350f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866/selection/1ba333922f13b62416e7e7e170603b320d8c484f4d2bd3d927925ed306efe293" :answer/id #uuid "df41c6c3-3a00-5138-8a93-244385e7d4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e619283-44d5-5221-8403-3681fc222179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127866/selection/f0b130aae11871f8f940254091c645824b094093f8af351a9790e3a04cfe79fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-127866/selection/eda157d924643265f1a75a141081379a28abc5464ff0d5b66fe5078e6a946d39" "q-127866/selection/0a91f8a657eeb741a874acf8efeeecdbb5296f53af78027bc777d36c253a0f7f" "q-127866/selection/385c7015fb21b22ceeda96a5b8f2b18de42db67284bafba3fabd3361d6d5baf4" "q-127866/selection/f0b130aae11871f8f940254091c645824b094093f8af351a9790e3a04cfe79fa" "q-127866/selection/1ba333922f13b62416e7e7e170603b320d8c484f4d2bd3d927925ed306efe293"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127866" :question/id #uuid "e0ae544d-cc6c-5242-be1f-c4ab12022dac" :question/math-academy-id "q-127866" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(5,0,5),$ $B(6,-1,4),$ $C(9,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(6i-j+4k)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(9i+j)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =4i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot (-1))j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =6i+j+5k \\\\  & =⟨6,1,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127866/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127866"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "ffbf30c9-fde6-52d3-90f6-80b647c79029" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913/selection/583c73d7342bb1dca635f3d7c25b82169d5404007ef3a58f5091fa40ef5cbc40" :answer/id #uuid "8408df31-3fe1-5752-8503-f5d07118e7dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{13}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913/selection/2c51ed624fe9e1fecb2612465e7246eb113be0451af08f26419fc6a4ed24c715" :answer/id #uuid "d02bc462-11d8-5f2f-98a9-6179d742bc6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{43}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913/selection/e290d10f618bf550949faf4b986b608e0c198958cea6ba48be6f6766be273724" :answer/id #uuid "e78d5b93-9a7c-5263-9f42-b9de8e15d0e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913/selection/97d9d6558078c35c1a1ecc785f0cc5cf0e0b50a9dee567db2f95e9184c2bed2d" :answer/id #uuid "a0a7ef88-bafd-52d8-8010-4d6ad00433d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bd5fe01-556a-5401-9f5b-cd3aa2173cd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127913/selection/97d9d6558078c35c1a1ecc785f0cc5cf0e0b50a9dee567db2f95e9184c2bed2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-127913/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-127913/selection/583c73d7342bb1dca635f3d7c25b82169d5404007ef3a58f5091fa40ef5cbc40" "q-127913/selection/2c51ed624fe9e1fecb2612465e7246eb113be0451af08f26419fc6a4ed24c715" "q-127913/selection/e290d10f618bf550949faf4b986b608e0c198958cea6ba48be6f6766be273724" "q-127913/selection/97d9d6558078c35c1a1ecc785f0cc5cf0e0b50a9dee567db2f95e9184c2bed2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127913" :question/id #uuid "bcadbcc6-c165-55d2-8f6d-17233cd5b6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-127913" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(6,1,5),$ $Q(5,1,7),$ $R(4,2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(5i+j+7k)-(6i+j+5k) \\\\  & =-i+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(4i+2j)-(6i+j+5k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot 2)i-((-1)\\cdot (-5)-(-2)\\cdot 2)j+((-1)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-2i-9j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-9,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{86}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127913/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127913"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316363/field-1/1ba333922f13b62416e7e7e170603b320d8c484f4d2bd3d927925ed306efe293" :answer/id #uuid "d5542b62-931d-5c25-bb57-e4e8ebd7be61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316363/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f9b6f94-0923-592c-ab85-2c159692018f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316363/field-1/1ba333922f13b62416e7e7e170603b320d8c484f4d2bd3d927925ed306efe293" :answer-field/choices ["q-316363/field-1/1ba333922f13b62416e7e7e170603b320d8c484f4d2bd3d927925ed306efe293"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316363" :question/id #uuid "0d66abf8-30b0-5105-912a-6d4e45ab575e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316363" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(-3,0,1)$, $M(0,2,-2)$, $N(2,-1,0).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2j-2k)-(-3i+k) \\\\  & =3i+2j-3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(2i-j)-(-3i+k) \\\\  & =5i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(3\\cdot (-1)-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(3\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-5i-12j-13k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-12,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-12)^{2}+(-13)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+144+169} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{338} \\\\  & =13\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316363/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316363"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316530/field-1/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "875f8dcb-5039-5964-ba26-3f56de0ce03a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316530/field-1/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" :answer/id #uuid "ec7e58ae-973a-546c-83e8-dd818521ee60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316530/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "851d5934-360b-5f83-a502-7978cec33428" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316530/field-1/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer-field/choices ["q-316530/field-1/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-316530/field-1/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316530" :question/id #uuid "ffc323ce-db7c-5144-9dd9-04891b843444" :question/math-academy-id "q-316530" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,STU,$ if $S(0,1,2),$ $T(2,3,1),$ $U(4,1,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST} & =t-s \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =u-s \\\\  & =(4i+j+2k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =4i+0j+0k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =0i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,STU$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316530/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316530"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316361/field-1/721d82afe492fced1ed61892e8c00f993dd38df4d01b60acced16e47a28c4bd3" :answer/id #uuid "a7dafd26-e1c8-5988-b5fd-f358198d6a5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316361/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a72c8e6-54f1-5a2a-8a9e-82f08199c327" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316361/field-1/721d82afe492fced1ed61892e8c00f993dd38df4d01b60acced16e47a28c4bd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-316361/field-1/721d82afe492fced1ed61892e8c00f993dd38df4d01b60acced16e47a28c4bd3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316361" :question/id #uuid "302af101-69b5-5e33-9c9d-a9141adebbf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316361" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,PQR$, if $P(1,-2,0)$, $Q(3,1,-1)$, $R(-1,0,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(3i+j-k)-(i-2j) \\\\  & =2i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(-i+2k)-(i-2j) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2)i-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-2))j+(2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =8i-2j+10k \\\\  & =⟨8,-2,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{168} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{42}}{2}=\\sqrt{42}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316361/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275225/field-1/a2f26a12fceafa23a072f976427e654ff8f8aa0ca09a6e8d28eeacfa10f47f20" :answer/id #uuid "55a9cdc3-3833-56f4-a3da-dd76e13921e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275225/field-1/58c29d4d22c63fb37e058b4eac66fcb74c289317ea7fc14917e5489311f1b759" :answer/id #uuid "1253243a-eac3-5cb7-9453-0078bf32091b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275225/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c1bcbd9-c2a5-50d2-bfad-900ea89dec66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275225/field-1/a2f26a12fceafa23a072f976427e654ff8f8aa0ca09a6e8d28eeacfa10f47f20" :answer-field/choices ["q-275225/field-1/a2f26a12fceafa23a072f976427e654ff8f8aa0ca09a6e8d28eeacfa10f47f20" "q-275225/field-1/58c29d4d22c63fb37e058b4eac66fcb74c289317ea7fc14917e5489311f1b759"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275225" :question/id #uuid "370d2d9d-9da0-5ac7-82a8-fa08d76b3133" :question/math-academy-id "q-275225" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(0,-2,-1)$, $C(-3,-2,0).$\n\n$CH=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j-k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-3i-2j)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-2i-2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{2}=\\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275225/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117/selection/d9efae05cd3b12211e1969b5fd54420e6e93a0948f54348ed4285d775e3ec16f" :answer/id #uuid "f9ee416a-3a31-5fa2-b09e-61dabf4886cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117/selection/5f15929055cb5f690c5ff40891c7343c5c174dc5706b23f49299f92fc04bfbc7" :answer/id #uuid "f4f5f81a-f178-5992-b43b-ba505092a6bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117/selection/b90bb3fe7362d482a5d4efc356c87f812928715d884d3233f853c02014abbbd2" :answer/id #uuid "38be1a1d-6c83-59fc-9d94-7dfe0b07a8df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{38}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "9e0a5989-2a01-5547-b2ad-1a642fbfaf02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117/selection/f9a6838dee8cbb373a1770489dce29265d6ecdd1902e7386ba7ff6a438ecc593" :answer/id #uuid "67a2c51e-8901-56b1-9ad8-079bfaee1fea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{38}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "87fcf33b-1e12-5e0d-9d55-336ec18e0985" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71117/selection/d9efae05cd3b12211e1969b5fd54420e6e93a0948f54348ed4285d775e3ec16f" :answer-field/choices ["q-71117/selection/d9efae05cd3b12211e1969b5fd54420e6e93a0948f54348ed4285d775e3ec16f" "q-71117/selection/5f15929055cb5f690c5ff40891c7343c5c174dc5706b23f49299f92fc04bfbc7" "q-71117/selection/b90bb3fe7362d482a5d4efc356c87f812928715d884d3233f853c02014abbbd2" "q-71117/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-71117/selection/f9a6838dee8cbb373a1770489dce29265d6ecdd1902e7386ba7ff6a438ecc593"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71117" :question/id #uuid "d006b7d2-a70b-5ccc-98ad-b02bab0dced5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71117" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $GH$ of the $△\\,GSM$, if $S(1,-1,2)$, $G(-2,0,2)$, $M(1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $GH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,GSM$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM\n$$\n\nSo, to find $GH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{SG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SM}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SG} & =g-s \\\\  & =(-2i+2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+j \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SM} & =m-s \\\\  & =(i+j)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SM} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0)i-((-3)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0)j+((-3)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =-2i-6j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-6,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{SG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SM}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{SG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{76} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,GSM$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{19}}{2}=\\sqrt{19}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $SM$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}SM & =|\\overset{\\to }{SM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =GH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ GH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ GH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-71117/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71117"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-20027"] :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(2,1,2)$, $B(1,2,1)$, $C(3,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-1))j+((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "4e582e62-a6e2-5fc9-b046-e365eb8be857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "b71415b6-bdb3-59ec-98cc-5ca2a76696e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "f24ed152-48c9-5112-ac63-ffbae641cdb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" :answer/id #uuid "fd63060e-0dc1-5d89-ae41-9511cffb6b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "7bc59802-053a-5c53-9ca8-1db0cfbd2617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16f3d069-f8a2-577c-99d6-a8187410b9a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128013/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer-field/choices ["q-128013/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-128013/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-128013/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" "q-128013/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" "q-128013/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128013" :question/id #uuid "34a477f8-24ad-5965-9464-d4bdb9c1c3ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-128013" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $MH$ of the $△\\,LMN,$ if $L(-1,4,1),$ $M(0,3,4),$ $N(1,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $MH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN\n$$\n\nSo, to find $MH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(3j+4k)-(-i+4j+k) \\\\  & =i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(i+4j+2k)-(-i+4j+k) \\\\  & =2i+k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)i-(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 3)j+(1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-i+5j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LN$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =|\\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{30} & =MH\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ MH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ MH & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128013/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316556/field-1/f8d7b36e155e242a565b264400711657fad7be7eb67e433793e433bdb1779b62" :answer/id #uuid "0a90a41d-9202-5583-9920-80d0d5f5e9a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316556/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "648b91e3-1e66-5187-8e27-3dcf1d68007b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316556/field-1/f8d7b36e155e242a565b264400711657fad7be7eb67e433793e433bdb1779b62" :answer-field/choices ["q-316556/field-1/f8d7b36e155e242a565b264400711657fad7be7eb67e433793e433bdb1779b62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316556" :question/id #uuid "e65dc510-2fb4-57f3-a150-1a3f75e0f8be" :question/math-academy-id "q-316556" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $HK$ of the $△\\,GHI,$ if $G(1,1,1),$ $H(3,2,4),$ $I(2,4,2).$\n\n$HK=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $HK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,GHI$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot GI\n$$\n\nSo, to find $HK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{GI}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GH}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GI} & =i-g \\\\  & =(2i+4j+2k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{GH} & =h-g \\\\  & =(3i+2j+4k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i+j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GI}\\times \\overset{\\to }{GH} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =8i-j-5k \\\\  & =⟨8,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{GI}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GH}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{GI}\\times \\overset{\\to }{GH}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,GHI$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $GI$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}GI & =|\\overset{\\to }{GI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot GI,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot \\sqrt{11} \\\\ HK & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ HK & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316556/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4344"] :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,0,-3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-1,2 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-3i-23j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-23,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-23)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{554}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA_{\\triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{554}}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4345"] :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ if $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(-2,0,1),$ $C(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(-3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0)j+(-3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4346"] :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0),$ $B(1,1,2),$ $C(1,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude (height) can be related to the area of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding altitude of the triangle.\n\nFor the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ we have $h=CH,$ and $b=AB.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =4i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula $A_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
